Package: HOME
Title: Harmonized Orphanhood Mortality Estimation
Version: 0.1.2
Authors@R: 
    person("Tamara", "Vaz",
           email = "tamaravaz.m@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements indirect methods for estimating adult mortality from
    orphanhood data: the Brass and Hill (1973) method, the regression-based
    method of Timaeus (1992) <https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12317481/>,
    and the extended orphanhood method of Luy (2012)
    <doi:10.1007/s13524-012-0101-4> for low-mortality populations. Besides
    the coefficients published by Luy for Italy, the package derives
    context-specific coefficients (weighting factors, reference-period
    parameters and the conversion of the mean age at childbearing of
    surviving parents to that of all parents) for any population and survey
    date from user-supplied period fertility, population, cohort mortality
    and period life table data, following the procedure of Luy (2009) <https://www.oeaw.ac.at/fileadmin/subsites/Institute/VID/PDF/Publications/EDRP/edrp_2009_03.pdf>.
    Estimates are harmonized into comparable adult mortality indicators
    (30q30, 45q15 and e30) with a relational logit model, and diagnostic
    tools assess the sensitivity of results to the mean age at childbearing
    and to the choice of model life table family.
